<title>GERMANY: Cologne air cargo rises 3.8 pct in March.</title>
<headline>Cologne air cargo rises 3.8 pct in March.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total flown air cargo handled at Cologne/Bonn airport (CGN) rose 3.8 percent in March 1997 to 29,759 tonnes, figures from the German airports association ADV showed.</p>
<p>Total flown cargo increased 2.8 percent to 83,578 tonnes in the first quarter of 1997, the monthly ADV traffic report showed.</p>
<p>Cargo handled at Cologne airport in March and for the year to date in tonnes and with year-on-year percentage changes includes:</p>
<p>  Mar 1997		   Monthly total	Pct change</p>
<p>  Total flown cargo	  29,759		Up   3.8</p>
<p>  Exports			14,298		Up   5.5</p>
<p>  Imports			14,626		Down 1.1</p>
<p>  Transit			   835		    n/a</p>
<p>  (Trucked cargo		1,664		    n/a)</p>
<p>  Jan-Mar 1997	    Cumulative total    Pct change</p>
<p>  Total flown cargo	  83,578		Up   2.8</p>
<p>  Exports			40,376		Up   5.6</p>
<p>  Imports			40,480		Down 2.7</p>
<p>  Transit			 2,722		    n/a</p>
<p>  (Trucked cargo		5,417		    n/a)</p>
<p>Source: German Airports Association ADV, market research dept. - Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom. Tel +44 171 542 7706 Fax+ 5017</p>
</text>
